<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Klungkung</h1><p class="st-meta">1686 CE – 1908 CE · capital Klungkung</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Senior royal house of Bali, heir to Gelgel, whose Dewa Agung was recognised as paramount king of the island until the puputan of 1908.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After a revolt destroyed the court of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gelgel">Gelgel</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dewa-agung-jambe">Dewa Agung Jambe</a> re-established the main Balinese dynasty at Klungkung (Semarapura) in 1686. Though other kingdoms such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-karangasem">Karangasem</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-buleleng">Buleleng</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-badung">Badung</a> became stronger, they still acknowledged the Dewa Agung as first among the rajas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, the heir of the Majapahit-descended kings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Klungkung was small, but its ruler held ritual primacy and presided over Balinese law and ceremonial. The court built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertha-gosa">Kertha Gosa</a> hall of justice, whose painted ceilings in the Kamasan style survive. In 1849 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dewa-agung-istri-kanya">Dewa Agung Istri Kanya</a>, a woman ruler, led resistance at Kusamba, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andreas-victor-michiels">Andreas Michiels</a> was killed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> invaded in April 1908, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dewa-agung-jambe-ii">Dewa Agung Jambe II</a> led his family and followers into a puputan, a ritual suicidal march into rifle fire. Klungkung was annexed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>, and later restored as a regency under the descendants of the royal house.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1686 CE – 1908 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.25%;width:4.42%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1686 CE – 1908 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Klungkung</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dewa Agung Jambe I, Dewa Agung Istri Kanya, Dewa Agung Jambe II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Balinese Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Balinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Klungkung, Semarapura</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1797&amp;focus=kingdom-of-klungkung" aria-label="Kingdom of Klungkung on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7869 2497 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Klungkung lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8189 2753L8189 2753M8189 2753L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8189 2753h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8189 2753h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8189 2753h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Klungkung. <a href="/atlas?year=1797&amp;focus=kingdom-of-klungkung">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
